    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bau9",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sau8",
          "text": "If applicable, wrongful death expenses",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "baub",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "saua",
          "text": "Partial Fault After a Denver Bicycle Accident",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "baud",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sauc",
          "text": "A common defense to bicycle accident claims that could reduce the financial compensation you receive is the modified comparative negligence defense. This argument could diminish your financial award by an amount that matches your percentage of fault for the accident. If the other driver can prove that you contributed to the accident, such as by running a stop sign or failing to pay attention to where you were riding, this can reduce your monetary recovery accordingly.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bauf",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "saue",
          "text": "Your financial recovery will be reduced by an amount that is equivalent to your degree of fault, but only to a maximum amount. Under Colorado’s modified version of this law, a plaintiff can only be found up to 49 percent responsible for an accident to still remain eligible for compensation. With an equal or greater share of fault as the defendant, a plaintiff is barred from recovery entirely. This is why it’s important to have an attorney represent your side of the case if you believe you contributed to your bike crash.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bauh",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "saug",
          "text": "Safety Tips for Bicycle Riders",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bauj",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "saui",
          "text": "While motor vehicle drivers are responsible for causing most bicycle accidents in Denver, there are things that you can do as a cyclist to decrease your risk of getting into a collision. Being proactive about your safety as a biker could save your life. Use these safety tips for bicyclists in Colorado to protect yourself from being hit by a car as much as possible:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "baul",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sauk",
          "text": "Obey the rules of the road. Traffic laws are in place to keep everyone safe. You can reduce your risk of an accident by obeying the laws that apply to you, such as coming to a complete stop at red lights and stop signs. Obeying the law keeps your movements predictable to surrounding drivers, reducing your odds of a collision.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "baun",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "saum",
          "text": "Signal your intentions. Don’t make drivers guess where you’re going. Use hand signals to indicate that you plan on turning. Letting other drivers know your intentions can allow them to move out of your way or wait for you to pass before proceeding.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "baup",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sauo",
          "text": "Be as visible as possible. Many bicycle accidents occur because the driver doesn’t see the bicyclist. Improve your visibility by biking in bright colors or wearing a reflective vest. Avoid riding your bicycle at night in Denver. If you must ride at night, make sure your bicycle has the required headlamp and rear light or reflector.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "baur",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sauq",
          "text": "If you get injured in a bike accident despite your best efforts to stay safe, you have legal rights. Discuss your options for seeking financial compensation and holding a driver accountable with a bike accident attorney at Dormer Harpring for more information. We offer free initial consultations and are passionate about improving the safety of Denver’s bicyclists.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "baut",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "saus",
          "text": "What to Do After a Denver Bike Accident",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bauv",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sauu",
          "text": "If you get injured in a Denver bike accident, check yourself for injuries and move out of harm’s way. Leave your bicycle where it is until photographs can be taken of the crash scene. If you are unable to move due to serious injuries, wait for paramedics to arrive. Otherwise, take the following steps:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bauy",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sauw",
          "text": "Call the police.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "saux",
          "text": " Report the bicycle accident to law enforcement by calling 911 immediately. Write down your police report number before the police leave the scene.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bav1",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sauz",
          "text": "Get medical care without delay.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sav0",
          "text": " You may have a concussion or internal injury that is not immediately apparent. Go to a hospital right away for treatment.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bav4",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sav2",
          "text": "Do not admit fault or apologize for the accident.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sav3",
          "text": " Do not say you are sorry or confess to contributing to the accident when speaking to the driver or the police.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bav7",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sav5",
          "text": "Exchange information with the driver who struck you.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sav6",
          "text": " Get the driver’s name, address, phone number, insurance information and a description of the vehicle.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bava",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sav8",
          "text": "Write down your version of events.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sav9",
          "text": " Document what happened while the details are still fresh in your mind. Give the police your side of the story for the report.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bavd",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "savb",
          "text": "Speak to eyewitnesses.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "savc",
          "text": " If anyone witnessed the bicycle accident, get their names and contact information. Eyewitness information is especially critical if it was a hit-and-run accident.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bavg",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "save",
          "text": "Take photographs.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "savf",
          "text": " Before you leave the scene, take pictures to document the collision. Look around for traffic or surveillance video cameras, as well.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bavj",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "savh",
          "text": "Document everything.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "savi",
          "text": " While you recover from the accident, keep copies of all medical records, hospital bills, property repair costs, travel expenses, lost wages and communications from insurance companies.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bavl",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "savk",
          "text": "When you are ready to pursue financial compensation for your bike accident, start by consulting with an attorney. Do not negotiate with insurance companies on your own. Hire a bicycle accident attorney in Denver to negotiate on your behalf to prevent an insurer from taking advantage of you.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
